  "question": {
    "text": "The rate of a reaction triples when temperature changes from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>20</mn><mn>0</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>50</mn><mn>0</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The energy of activation for the reaction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>"
  },
